;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.3.2 Tool Result Optimization: how tool outputs are shrunk before they enter the conversation: per-tool summaries, offloading of very large outputs, hints, and their link to compaction
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/03_context-engineering/03_context-engineering.lisp / s8 .. s13
;;; members: problem summarizer offload hints compaction-link design-evolution
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: none
(defrule tool-result -> tool-result-problem tool-result-summarizer tool-result-offload tool-result-hints tool-result-compaction-link tool-result-design-evolution)
(defrule tool-result-problem -> :nucleus tool-result-problem/n :elaboration-additional tool-result-problem/a1 :elaboration-additional tool-result-problem/a2 :elaboration-additional tool-result-problem/a3)
(defrule tool-result-problem/n -> :instruction "生の出力が文脈を食いつぶす様子を 1 文で書く" :sample "Raw tool outputs consume far more tokens than their informational value warrants.")
(defrule tool-result-problem/a1 -> :instruction "具体的な大きさの例を 1 文で書く" :sample "A single read_file may return 2,000–3,000 tokens of source code, a directory listing may enumerate hundreds of entries, and a test-runner invocation may produce thousands of lines of TAP output.")
(defrule tool-result-problem/a2 -> :instruction "放置した場合の結果を 1 文で書く" :sample "Left unchecked, verbose results dominate the context window within a few iterations, crowding out the user query and system instructions that drive the agent’s behavior.")
(defrule tool-result-problem/a3 -> :instruction "対策の考え方を 1 文で書く" :sample "Tool result optimization addresses this by transforming raw outputs into compact, semantically preserving representations before they enter the conversation history.")
(defrule tool-result-summarizer -> :nucleus tool-result-summarizer/n :elaboration-set-member tool-result-summarizer/a1)
(defrule tool-result-summarizer/n -> :instruction "結果ごとの要約器の働きを 1 文で書く" :sample "Each tool result passes through a dedicated summarizer that maps the tool name and raw output to a concise summary (typically 50–200 characters).")
(defrule tool-result-summarizer/a1 -> :instruction "道具の種類ごとの縮め方を 1 項目ずつ、種類と縮めた後の姿で書く" :sample "File reads are replaced with metadata: “ ✓ Read file (142 lines, 4,831 chars) ”. The full content remains available through re-reading, but the context carries only the proof that the read occurred and the file’s approximate size. / Search results report match counts rather than matched lines: “ ✓ Search completed (23 matches found) ”. When a search returns no results, the summary reflects this explicitly so the agent can redirect. / Directory listings are collapsed to item counts: “ ✓ Listed directory (47 items) ”. The raw listing, which often contains deeply nested paths, is replaced by a single-line summary. / Command execution adapts to output length: short outputs (≤ 100 characters) are retained verbatim; longer outputs report line counts: “ ✓ Command executed (312 lines of output) ”. / Errors are truncated to 200 characters with a classified prefix: “ × Error: FileNotFoundError: ... ”. This ensures the agent receives enough information for error recovery (Section 2.3.5) without consuming excessive context on stack traces." :kind bullet)
(defrule tool-result-offload -> :nucleus tool-result-offload/n :elaboration-additional tool-result-offload/a1)
(defrule tool-result-offload/n -> :instruction "要約でも足りない大きな出力の扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "For outputs that exceed 8,000 characters (approximately 2,000 tokens), the summarizer is insufficient: the full output would still dominate the context even after summarization.")
(defrule tool-result-offload/a1 -> :instruction "置き換える内容と、全文を後で読めることで生まれる段階を 1〜2 文で書く" :sample "The system writes the full output to a session-specific scratch directory (~/.opendev/scratch/<session_id>/) and replaces the output in the conversation with a 500-character preview plus a reference path: “ [Output offloaded: 2,341 lines, 48,203 chars → <path>].")
(defrule tool-result-hints -> :nucleus tool-result-hints/n :elaboration-additional tool-result-hints/a1)
(defrule tool-result-hints/n -> :instruction "退避したときの案内が、エージェントの能力に合わせて変わることを 1 文で書く" :sample "When output is offloaded to a scratch file, the truncation message includes a tailored recovery hint based on the current agent’s capabilities.")
(defrule tool-result-hints/a1 -> :instruction "部下を使えるか使えないかで変わる案内と、その目的を 1〜2 文で書く" :sample "If the agent has access to subagent delegation (the spawn_subagent tool), the hint suggests: “ Delegate to a Code Explorer subagent to process the full output via search and read tools. ” If the agent lacks subagent capability (e.g., it is a subagent), the hint instead suggests: “ Use the search tool with offset/limit parameters to process the output incrementally. ” This agent-aware advice prevents the common failure mode where an agent attempts a recovery strategy unavailable in its tool set, for example, a Code Explorer subagent trying to spawn another subagent.")
(defrule tool-result-compaction-link -> :nucleus tool-result-compaction-link/n :elaboration-additional tool-result-compaction-link/a1 :elaboration-additional tool-result-compaction-link/a2)
(defrule tool-result-compaction-link/n -> :instruction "要約と退避が相補う役割を持つことを 1 文で書く" :sample "Tool result summaries and offloaded outputs serve complementary roles.")
(defrule tool-result-compaction-link/a1 -> :instruction "圧縮のときの使い方を 1 文で書く" :sample "During compaction (Section 2.3.6), the compactor preferentially uses pre-computed summaries when sanitizing messages for LLM-based summarization, avoiding redundant re-processing.")
(defrule tool-result-compaction-link/a2 -> :instruction "この組み合わせの効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "This synergy means that even when emergency compaction is triggered, the input to the summarizer LLM is already substantially compressed, improving both the speed and quality of the compaction output.")
(defrule tool-result-design-evolution -> :nucleus tool-result-design-evolution/n :elaboration-additional tool-result-design-evolution/a1 :elaboration-additional tool-result-design-evolution/a2 :elaboration-additional tool-result-design-evolution/a3)
(defrule tool-result-design-evolution/n -> :instruction "初期の版が出力をどう保存していたかと、その問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "Early versions stored full tool output in the conversation history regardless of length.")
(defrule tool-result-design-evolution/a1 -> :instruction "問題の具体例を 1 文で書く" :sample "A single long-running test suite could consume 30,000 tokens of context in one tool call.")
(defrule tool-result-design-evolution/a2 -> :instruction "要約器の効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "The per-tool summarizer reduced this to under 100 tokens in most cases.")
(defrule tool-result-design-evolution/a3 -> :instruction "退避の閾値を足した効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "Adding the 8,000-character offloading threshold addressed the remaining outliers (large file reads, verbose command outputs) that exceeded the summarizer’s compression ratio, extending typical session length from 15–20 turns (before context overflow) to 30–40 turns without compaction.")
